// Dialog :
"P2975776638" "Well done, {VillainName}. Are you wondering why you aren't seeing the changes in the time stream. You wouldn't, not yet. I however can. You are a rock rising out of the stream with all of possibility flowing around you."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P183839814" "You don't have to hide your thoughts from me. I can see them all over your face. You don't believe Manticore would turn against his kind. Very well, I have just the place for you to go next. You will see who Manticore is willing to become.<br><br>Are you interested in seeing this transformation?"
// AcceptString :
"P2173339037" "Determine the true depths of Manticore's evil ways."
// SendOffString :
"P952172897" "Recluse made a proposal to Manticore: take out <color deepskyblue>Sister Psyche</color>. If you had difficulty believing Manticore would turn on his own, you'll likely find this even harder to believe. So, go back in time and see what this man who claims to be a hero did and then tell me, is it the actions or the intention behind them that makes us heroes or villains?"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3968217577" "Aid Manticore against Sister Psyche"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P351123387" "You need to go with Manticore and help him take out Sister Psyche. Or, if he changes his mind, be there to witness what he does. The Arachnos will believe that you are working for Lord Recluse directly. They will give you no cause for worry."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P437020894" "<color deepskyblue>Part Two</color>"

